--TEST--
`Core\Task::all` refuses an array of callables, a shape whose fields are not callables, and a subject that is not a shape at all, naming the same expected type each time — `rule:concurrency/all-answers-a-typed-shape`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:concurrency/core-task-all-a-fixed-set-of-tasks
// An array of callables has no field names to answer under, so it is not the subject
// even though every element is a callable.
var $a = Core\Task::all([fn(): int => 1]);

// A shape whose field holds a value rather than a function has nothing to run.
var $b = Core\Task::all({rows: [1, 2, 3]});

// And a subject that is not a shape at all.
var $c = Core\Task::all("not a shape");
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `{name: callable(): T, ...}`, found `array<mixed>`
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
